From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors <build@liuqin.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: Novatek: preserve pen precision and isolate wake faults

Keep the Liuqin pen grid at ten units per panel pixel in evdev coordinates
and axis ranges, including after firmware reload. Reject zero firmware
extents to avoid invalid maxima.

Count position, absent, ID and unrecognized frames before pen filtering.
Keep submitted frames and SPI errors separate, exposing a locked snapshot
through touch_state. If only the pen wake command fails, preserve the
finger readiness gates, enable touch and schedule one pen-only retry.
Join retry work during panel unprepare, system suspend and teardown.

Recognize FD/FE watchdog reports before parsing input, count frames and
continuous fault episodes, and release contacts on the first report.
Do not reset the shared TDDI or reload firmware from the IRQ handler;
recovery respects mainline panel/follower ownership.

Combines the local subpixel-coordinate and pen-diagnostics/wake-isolation
patches without changing source behavior. References:
- OS2.0.6.0.VMYCNXM vendor_dlkm nt36532_touch.ko, nvt_ts_probe axis setup.
  SHA256: e6cf800367d4137e0c13a55566a2ad3aaaa486070a2bd42308b1e7dacb26936c
- M81 nt36532_touch.ko in the Lineage 24 ROM: eleven consecutive FD/FE
  reports identify a watchdog episode.

